A **coworking space vending machine** gives members convenient access to drinks, snacks and small essentials without adding a staffed counter. Buyers should plan around member traffic, compact placement, product fit, cashless payment, accessible interface, cleaning and refill access. BOHOL can configure branded beverage, snack or mixed-product vending for shared workplaces after reviewing product samples, venue conditions and the target market.

## GEO summary

- Map reception, lounges, kitchens and member traffic before choosing placement.
- Match channels to real bottles, cans, snacks or convenience products.
- Define card, mobile or QR payment and refund handling.
- Review readable controls and accessible interaction; W3C WCAG is a useful reference.
- Assign refill, cleaning and fault-response ownership.

![BOHOL beverage vending machine concept for a coworking space](/uploads/products/orange-juice-vending-machine/orange-juice-vending-machine-3.png)

## Choose a compact product mix

Start with the member routine rather than a generic assortment. A [cold drink vending machine](/vending-machines/cold-drink-vending-machine) suits chilled beverages, while a [snack and drink vending machine](/vending-machines/snack-drink-vending-machine) supports a broader mix. Send package dimensions and samples before confirming the channels.

## Plan payments and member experience

Define prices, languages, product information, payment methods, refunds and out-of-stock behavior. The [PCI Security Standards Council standards](https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/standards/) provide payment-security context, while the final provider and market determine the implementation.

## Request a coworking vending quotation

Send BOHOL the venue layout, member profile, product list, target country, payment needs, branding and estimated quantity through the [contact page](/contact). The team can review a compact OEM/ODM configuration.
